UID:future-vision-xprize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151547Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Future Vision XPRIZE (sci-fi film competition)
DESCRIPTION:Future Vision XPRIZE is a sci-fi film competition challenging f
 ilmmakers to portray an optimistic\, abundant future for humanity rather t
 han a dystopian one. CHALLENGE: create a 3-minute sci-fi trailer that depi
 cts a bold\, original\, hopeful vision of progress. PRIZES: USD 3.5 millio
 n-plus total\; the grand prize winner gets USD 2.6 million-plus to turn th
 eir trailer into a feature film\, plus over USD 1 million in prizes for ru
 nners-up. BACKGROUND: launched by the nonprofit XPRIZE and funded by Peter
  Diamandis\, with Google and Range as partners\; inspired by the optimism 
 of Star Trek and intended to give storytellers a hopeful 'north star' for 
 builders. ELIGIBILITY: open to all filmmakers globally. TIMELINE: competit
 ion launched 9 March 2026\; submission deadline 15 August 2026\; finals on
  25 September 2026 in Los Angeles (finalists attend in person). APPLY: reg
 ister and read the rules on the contest website at futurevisionxprize.com.
 \n\nOrganisation: XPRIZE (Future Vision XPRIZE\, funded by Peter Diamandis
 \; partners Google and Range)\nLocation: Online / Worldwide (finals held i
 n Los Angeles)\nAward: USD 3.5 million-plus prize pool. Grand prize winner
  receives USD 2.6 million-plus to develop their vision into a feature film
 \, with over USD 1 million in additional prizes for runners-up.\nDuration:
  One-off competition\; create a 3-minute sci-fi trailer\n\nMore: https://f
 uturevisionxprize.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://futurevisionxprize.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online / Worldwide (finals held in Los Angeles)
