UID:mountainfilm-commitment-grants-emerging-filmmaker-fellowship-2026@artif
 icialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151547Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260717
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mountainfilm: Commitment Grants & Emerging Filmmaker Fell
 owship
DESCRIPTION:Mountainfilm's Commitment Grants support documentary filmmakers
  with projects in post-production\, with over USD 90\,000 in funding this 
 cycle for films that celebrate adventure\, activism\, social justice\, cul
 ture\, the environment\, and indomitable spirit. Mountainfilm actively enc
 ourages diversity behind the camera\, and a portion of funding is set asid
 e for two focus areas: projects featuring an LGBTQ+ protagonist or a story
  about overcoming personal challenges\, societal stigmas\, and/or communit
 y obstacles with a meaningful connection to the outdoors or nature-based p
 ursuits\; and projects exploring immigration or migration\, or created by 
 immigrant or first-generation immigrant filmmakers. AWARDS: individual Com
 mitment Grants range from USD 3\,000 to 6\,000. EMERGING FILMMAKER FELLOWS
 HIP: one early-career filmmaker is selected from the Commitment Grant appl
 icant pool for a yearlong mentorship that includes edit and story consulta
 tion\, networking opportunities\, a cash award\, and a funded trip to Tell
 uride during the festival over Memorial Day weekend (travel\, lodging\, an
 d a Mountainfilm pass\, applicable to the year following the award). ELIGI
 BILITY: Commitment Grants are open to applicants from any country\; the Em
 erging Filmmaker Fellowship accepts applicants from any country but requir
 es current U.S. residency. Post-production projects only\, completed\, rel
 eased\, or festival-screened projects are not eligible\, and impact campai
 gns are not funded. Prior Commitment Grant recipients should not re-apply 
 for the same project\; previously declined projects may re-apply only with
  substantial changes. REQUIREMENTS: a video sample or trailer of the curre
 nt project no longer than 10 minutes (password-protected Vimeo links prefe
 rred)\; the screener link must stay active and cannot be changed after sub
 mission. The Emerging Filmmaker application additionally requires a direct
 or bio\, headshot\, and cover letter. Recipients are expected to provide p
 rogress updates 2-3 times a year\, include Mountainfilm recognition in cre
 dits\, and discuss premiere consideration with the programming team. TIMEL
 INE: applications are open July 1 to July 16\, 2026 (closing 11:59 PM MDT)
 \, with notifications in late August or early September. Questions: entrie
 s@mountainfilm.org.\n\nOrganisation: Mountainfilm\nLocation: Application o
 nline\; Telluride\, Colorado\, United States (fellowship trip during the f
 estival). Commitment Grants are open to filmmakers from any country\; the 
 Emerging Filmmaker Fellowship requires current U.S. residency.\nAward: Ove
 r USD 90\,000 in total funding. Individual Commitment Grants range from US
 D 3\,000 to 6\,000. The Emerging Filmmaker Fellowship adds a yearlong ment
 orship\, a cash award\, and a funded trip to Telluride over Memorial Day w
 eekend (travel\, lodging\, and a festival pass).\nDuration: Commitment Gra
 nts support projects in post-production\; the Emerging Filmmaker Fellowshi
 p is a yearlong mentorship.\n\nMore: https://www.mountainfilm.org/mountain
 film-initiatives/commitment-grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mountainfilm.org/mountainfilm-initiatives/commitment-grants
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Application online\; Telluride\, Colorado\, United States (fellows
 hip trip during the festival). Commitment Grants are open to filmmakers fr
 om any country\; the Emerging Filmmaker Fellowship requires current U.S. r
 esidency.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:web-residencies-no-22-ignore-all-previous-instructions-2026@artificialn
 ouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151547Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260807
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260808
SUMMARY:Deadline: Akademie Schloss Solitude: Web Residencies No. 22 - Ignor
 e All Previous Instructions
DESCRIPTION:Web Residencies No. 22\, 'Ignore All Previous Instructions\,' i
 s curated by !Mediengruppe Bitnik as part of Akademie Schloss Solitude's W
 eb Residencies program\, which since 2016 has supported young talents from
  the international digital scene as well as artists of all disciplines eng
 aging with web-based practices. For the tenth anniversary of the program\,
  this edition invites artists to create works that challenge extractive di
 gital platforms and AI systems\, exploring how to interrupt dominant techn
 ological logics\, from ad-tech surveillance to prompt injection vulnerabil
 ities\, and imagine alternative structures and communication methods. The 
 open call seeks proposals that hijack\, glitch\, and disrupt rather than c
 omply with existing systems\, drawing on strategies like Situationist deto
 urnement to map routes through and around the grids we are trapped within.
  Four to six proposals will be selected. BENEFITS: a four-week online resi
 dency\; a grant of EUR 1\,200\; a web space (microsite) on which the proje
 ct can be developed and published online\; support from a web/UX designer 
 and a programmer (in a supportive capacity only\, not to build an entire w
 ebsite)\; and participation in individual and group online events with the
  curators and Solitude fellows. Offline or hybrid formats (a reading sessi
 on\, panel\, exhibition\, or curated program) may follow. ELIGIBILITY: art
 ists of all disciplines may apply\, with no age limit\; submission is free
  of charge. The residency takes place exclusively online\, and selected fe
 llows agree to be available online during the four weeks. TIMELINE: the op
 en call runs from July 7 to August 7\, 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Akademie Sch
 loss Solitude\nLocation: Online (fully remote). Awarded by Akademie Schlos
 s Solitude\, Stuttgart\, Germany.\nAward: EUR 1\,200 grant for a four-week
  online residency\, plus a microsite to develop and publish the project\, 
 and support from a web/UX designer and a programmer in a supportive capaci
 ty.\nDuration: Four-week online residency.\n\nMore: https://application.ak
 ademie-solitude.de/fellowship-information/web-residencies?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://application.akademie-solitude.de/fellowship-information/web-res
 idencies?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online (fully remote). Awarded by Akademie Schloss Solitude\, Stut
 tgart\, Germany.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ecoslay-mag-02-urban-issue-open-call-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T151547Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260713
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260714
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ecoslay Mag: Open Call for Contributions\, Issue 02 "The 
 Urban Issue"
DESCRIPTION:Ecoslay Mag invites contributions for the second print issue of
  Ecoslay\, "The Urban Issue\," exploring the city as a space where interse
 ctional ecological futures are negotiated\, contested\, resisted\, and rei
 nvented. In the Ecoslay way\, pop culture and its influence are analysed a
 nd hijacked to communicate socio-ecological issues and ignite systemic cha
 nge: what happens when climate politics meets internet culture\, urban eco
 logy meets reality TV\, and sustainability discourse collides with camp\, 
 irony\, humour\, and memes. FORMATS (including but not limited to): essays
 \, interviews\, science communication\, poems\, visual art\, documentation
  of (art)works\, and fiction. TOPICS: urban climate communication through 
 humour\, memes\, and pop culture\; greenwashing\, eco-branding\, and susta
 inable aesthetics in urban contexts\; urban farming\, more-than-human life
 \, housing crises\, displacement and green gentrification\, class and the 
 city\, maintenance and care work in relation to urbanism\, urban environme
 ntal justice\, and community organizing\, and how these relate to pop cult
 ure\; and reflections on what Ecoslay means in an age of overlapping crise
 s. COMMITMENT: selected participants deliver one contribution to Issue 02 
 and attend two online workshops with the editorial team and fellow contrib
 utors for communal exchange and feedback on proposals and works-in-progres
 s. WHAT'S OFFERED: financial compensation for selected contributions\, edi
 torial support\, and edition\, proofreading\, and graphic design handled b
 y the team. TIMELINE: open call closes 13 July 2026\; selected contributor
 s announced approx. 15 August 2026\; work on contributions approx. 1 Septe
 mber 2026 to 10 January 2027\; contributor workshop approx. 15 September 2
 026\; final contribution deadline approx. 10 January 2027. HOW TO APPLY: s
 ubmit via the Google form. Questions via ecoslay@protonmail.com or Instagr
 am DM @ecoslay_mag.\n\nOrganisation: Ecoslay Mag\nLocation: Remote / inter
 national. Two online workshops with the editorial team\; contributions del
 ivered remotely.\nAward: Financial compensation for selected contributions
  (amount unspecified). Editorial support\, proofreading\, and graphic desi
 gn provided. No application fee.\nDuration: Contributions developed approx
 . 1 September 2026 to 10 January 2027\, with two online workshops (first a
 round 15 September 2026). Final contribution deadline approx. 10 January 2
 027.\n\nMore: https://ecoslay-mag.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral#open-call
URL:https://ecoslay-mag.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral#open-call
LOCATION:Remote / international. Two online workshops with the editorial te
 am\; contributions delivered remotely.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ryse-innovation-hub-youth-innovation-advisor-2026@artificialnouveau.git
